  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Geared for Success (GFS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Canada recently launched a call for concept notes on education for refugee and displaced children and youth. The call seeks to improve their learning outcomes. In particular, Canada aims to help girls and adolescent girls living in partner countries of sub-Saharan Africa. The call is open to Canadian organizations. They must have the capacity to implement education programming for refugee and displaced children and youth. They must also work with and improve the capacity of local organizations:
https://www.international.gc.ca/world-monde/funding-financement/call-education-appel.aspx?lang=eng

Outcomes provided by GAC:
&#xf0fc; Ultimate outcome: enhanced equitable and inclusive learning outcomes for refugee, internally displaced and host community children and youth, particularly girls and adolescent girls
&#xf0fc; Intermediate outcomes:
a. improved performance of local refugee and/or IDP-led organizations working on gender-responsive education
b. increased access to gender-responsive quality education for refugees and internally displaced children and youth, particularly girls and adolescent girls, enabled by refugee and/or IDP-led organizations
c. enhanced collective action of local refugee and/or IDP-led organizations (including women-led/rights organizations) to advance the right to gender-responsive quality education for refugee and internally displaced children and youth, particularly vulnerable groups
&#xf0fc; Additional preferences:
d. Include dynamic partnerships of Canadian organizations
e. Empower and engage local voices, actors and community-based organizations, in particular refugee-led and IDP-led organizations, throughout the project cycle
f. Pursue a learning agenda informedby research and monitoring and evaluation, and establisha community of practice with other successful applicants of this call, their partners and other relevant stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
